NEARS-2305 QA (2026-08-25, emulator-5554) — control repro proving the
"stale address + spurious not-in-zone banner" symptom is a PRE-EXISTING,
GENERAL defect UNRELATED to the _restoredTarget/TB-2305-2 mechanism.

Repro (zero restore/picker involvement):
1. Fresh Vendor Registration -> Location Info, no zone picked yet.
2. Real tap on the embedded Google Map (sets _hasUserInteractedWithMap=true,
   marker at the seeded default position, ~Dhaka-area coords) -> correctly
   shows "Please place the marker inside the zones" (expected: default
   position genuinely isn't in any zone).
3. Real dropdown pick "Abu Dhabi Zone" (no picker visit, no restore, no
   _restoredTarget ever set this session).

Observed: zone selection correctly updates to "Abu Dhabi Zone" (the fresh
pick), but the address/banner PERSISTS frozen on "Q9Q4+726, Dhaka,
Bangladesh" / "Please place the marker inside the zones" indefinitely
(re-checked after 5s+, never self-corrects). No [FAIL]/[ERR] logged for
this specific freeze (unlike the separate crash below).

This is IDENTICAL in shape to the symptom NEARS-2305/TB-2305-2 describes,
but reproduces with NO restore-grace race possible (selectedZoneIndex was
never frozen -- it always tracks the picked zone correctly; only the
address/banner's self-correction via _setPolygon's delayed animateCamera
-> onCameraIdle -> suppress-flag refresh chain never completes). A prior
QA cycle on this same ticket already flagged an adjacent symptom as
"regression-candidate-getzoneid-race.log" (see sibling file, 08-25 04:53).

Separately, an aggressive (<300ms) pick-after-restore attempt hit an
UNCAUGHT StateError from the SAME _setPolygon.animateCamera call site
(see bug-mapcontroller-disposed-crash.log/.png):
  "Bad state: GoogleMapController for map ID 2 was used after the
  associated GoogleMap widget had already been disposed."
  at select_location_view_widget.dart:762 (_setPolygon's Future.delayed
  animateCamera call) -- unguarded by `mounted`/try-catch unlike sibling
  call sites in the same file.

Neither of these is touched by fd2732f3 (a clean 2-line
`_restoredTarget = null;` insertion, verified via `git show`); both
reproduce identically whether or not the fix is present, since the
freeze/crash happens via a call path (_setPolygon) that fix does not
modify. Filed as regression_bugs, not blocking NEARS-2305.
